# --- Which Supabase project this build talks to ---
# THE URL AND THE KEY ARE A MATCHED PAIR. The publishable ("anon") key is a JWT
# whose `ref` claim names the project it belongs to, so a URL from one project
# and a key from another authenticate to nothing. src/integrations/supabase/env.ts
# therefore resolves them together: set BOTH or set NEITHER. Setting one alone
# uses both built-in defaults instead of mixing them, and says so on the console.
#
# Unset, a build behaves exactly as it did when these values were written into
# 31 source files by hand — the project below is the built-in fallback.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://dduzbchuswwbefdunfct.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImRkdXpiY2h1c3d3YmVmZHVuZmN0Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NTU0NDM4NzksImV4cCI6MjA3MTAxOTg3OX0.eSYU6fxIc3tBQuGLsdBRff0alBMkNfvv7OpW0efNjxk"

# Server-side (Edge Functions / scripts). Not read by the browser bundle.
SUPABASE_URL="https://dduzbchuswwbefdunfct.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImRkdXpiY2h1c3d3YmVmZHVuZmN0Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NTU0NDM4NzksImV4cCI6MjA3MTAxOTg3OX0.eSYU6fxIc3tBQuGLsdBRff0alBMkNfvv7OpW0efNjxk"

# LEGACY, and deliberately no longer read by any live call site. It was a THIRD
# name for the same project, free to disagree with the two above — unset, the
# one page that composed a URL from it fetched `https://undefined.supabase.co`.
# The project ref is now DERIVED from VITE_SUPABASE_URL (SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF).
# Do not reintroduce a call site that reads it.
# VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="dduzbchuswwbefdunfct"

# --- Workspace identity & support ---
# VITE_AURIXA_BILLING_UID identifies this workspace to Aurixa Mission Control
# (entitlements, billing, and the support portal handoff). Defaults to
# "npc-prime" when unset — see src/hooks/useWorkspaceEntitlements.tsx and
# src/lib/missionControl.ts.
# VITE_AURIXA_BILLING_UID="npc-prime"

# Base URL of the Aurixa Systems Support Portal opened from the Support page.
# Trailing slashes are stripped; workspace/user identity is appended as query
# parameters. Defaults to https://www.aurixasystems.com.au/support when unset.
# VITE_SUPPORT_PORTAL_URL="https://www.aurixasystems.com.au/support"

# --- Turnstile (the login CAPTCHA) ---
# The site key of this deployment's own Cloudflare Turnstile widget. A widget
# is a (site key, secret) pair: this value is public and is rendered by the
# browser, and its twin `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY` is a Supabase function secret
# that `siteverify` checks the token against. The two must come from the SAME
# widget or every sign-in is refused with `invalid-input-secret`.
#
# Unset, this deployment uses its built-in site key — but ONLY while it is
# talking to the Supabase project that key's secret lives in. A build pointed
# at another project (a mirror, a clone) resolves to no key at all and says so,
# rather than rendering this deployment's widget on somebody else's login page.
# That is not hypothetical: the key used to be a literal in
# src/components/auth/TurnstileWidget.tsx and npc-client-dashboard inherited it
# verbatim. See src/lib/turnstileSiteKey.ts.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="0x4AAAA..."

# --- Client-facing deployment mode ---
# When "true", the build hides developer/operator tooling (Integrations
# credential cards, Workflow Playground, engine diagnostics, test-data
# controls) from navigation AND routing, and disables the pricing-mock
# toggle. Build-time only — no URL or localStorage override, by design.
# Visibility only, never access control; see docs/CLIENT_FACING_MODE.md
# and src/lib/clientFacing.ts. Defaults to off (the internal console).
# VITE_CLIENT_FACING="true"

# --- Internal test data (never set on a client-facing build) ---
# Comma-separated phone numbers pre-filled in the Call Logs cleanup control.
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the browser bundle, so whatever is
# set here is public — which is exactly why it is a variable now. Two real
# staff mobiles used to be written into
# src/components/call-logs/CleanupTestCalls.tsx and shipped in every build,
# readable by anyone who opened the app, including deployments that hide the
# control (hiding a button does not unship the module it lives in).
#
# Unset, the list is empty and an operator adds numbers by hand in the popover
# exactly as before. Use test numbers here, never a real person's.
# VITE_TEST_CALL_NUMBERS="+61400000000,+61400000001"

# --- Server-side vendor secrets (Supabase Edge Function secrets, NEVER VITE_) ---
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the browser bundle by Vite and is
# therefore public. Vendor keys belong in the Supabase project's function
# secrets instead:
#
#   supabase secrets set GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY=...
#
# GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY backs the `google-fonts-catalog` edge function, which is
# the only thing that may hold it. Template Builder's font picker previously
# called googleapis.com from the browser with this key written into
# src/hooks/useGoogleFonts.ts, so it shipped in every build. Without the secret
# set, the picker falls back to its curated list — degraded, not broken.

# --- MCP tooling (local dev only, NOT bundled into the app) ---
# API key for the @21st-dev/magic MCP server referenced in .mcp.json as ${MAGIC_API_KEY}.
# Generate one at https://21st.dev/magic/console, then copy this file to .env.local and
# fill in the value (or export MAGIC_API_KEY in your shell before starting Claude Code).
# Leave blank here — never commit a real key.
MAGIC_API_KEY=""

# API key for the hosted `21st` HTTP MCP server referenced in .mcp.json as
# ${TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY}. Sent as the `x-api-key` request header. Generate one at
# https://21st.dev/magic/console, then copy this file to .env.local and fill in the
# value (or export TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY in your shell before starting Claude Code).
# Leave blank here — never commit a real key.
TWENTY_FIRST_API_KEY=""
